{% extends 'base.html.twig' %}

{% block title %}Sensitive page - Symfony 8.2 oidc_login{% endblock %}

{% block body %}
<main>
    <a class="back" href="{{ path('app_home') }}">&larr; Back to the scenario list</a>

    <header class="top-bar">
        <div class="title">
            <p class="eyebrow">firewall <code>reauth</code></p>
            <h1>Sensitive page</h1>
            <p class="summary">This page requires <code>IS_AUTHENTICATED_VERY_RECENTLY</code>, through the <code>#[IsGranted]</code> attribute of its controller: your last proof of identity must be younger than {{ lifetime }} seconds (<code>very_recent_authentication_lifetime</code>).</p>
        </div>
        <div class="session">
            <div class="session-actions">
                {% if user %}<span class="pill">{{ user.preferredUsername ?? user.userIdentifier }}</span>{% endif %}
                <a class="button" href="{{ path('_logout_reauth') }}">Log out</a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </header>

    <section class="card">
        <h3>Your proofs of identity</h3>
        <table class="value-table">
            <tbody>
                {% for method, time in proofs %}
                    <tr>
                        <th><code>{{ method }}</code></th>
                        <td>{{ time|date('H:i:s T') }}, {{ now - time }} seconds ago{% if method == '*' %} <span class="text-muted">(unspecified: Keycloak names no amr method)</span>{% endif %}</td>
                    </tr>
                {% endfor %}
                <tr>
                    <th><code>oidc_acr</code></th>
                    <td>
                        {{ acr ?? 'none' }}
                        {% if acr == '1' %}<span class="text-muted">Keycloak checked your password during the last login</span>
                        {% elseif acr == '0' %}<span class="text-muted">Keycloak answered from its session, no password typed</span>
                        {% endif %}
                    </td>
                </tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
        <p class="meaning">
            The proof time is the <code>auth_time</code> claim of the ID token, the moment Keycloak last checked your password. A login answered from an existing Keycloak session carries that older time: if it is already past {{ lifetime }} seconds, this page asks for your password right after such a login.
        </p>
        <p class="meaning">
            Reload after {{ lifetime }} seconds: the vote denying <code>IS_AUTHENTICATED_VERY_RECENTLY</code> asks for a re-authentication, and instead of a 403 the firewall hands the request to the oidc_login authenticator, which sends you to Keycloak with <code>prompt=login</code> and your ID token as <code>id_token_hint</code>, then back to this page.
        </p>
        <div class="chips">
            <a class="button" href="{{ path('app_reauth_sensitive') }}">Reload</a>
            <a class="button button-quiet" href="{{ path('app_account', {firewall: 'reauth'}) }}">Account page and flow trace</a>
        </div>
    </section>
</main>
{% endblock %}
